---
import MarketLayout from "../../../../layouts/MarketLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../../../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { SITE_ORIGIN, vancouver } from "../../../../data/site";

const path = `${vancouver.path}/buildings/who-pays/`;
---

<MarketLayout
  title="Who Pays for Strata Water Damage in BC | Tidemark"
  description="Strata corporation vs owner, deductibles, and chargebacks. General guidance, not legal advice."
  path={path}
>
  <main id="main">
    <div class="wrap">
      <Breadcrumbs
        crumbs={[
          { name: "Tidemark", href: `${SITE_ORIGIN}${vancouver.path}/` },
          { name: "Buildings", href: `${SITE_ORIGIN}${vancouver.path}/buildings/` },
          { name: "Who pays" },
        ]}
      />
    </div>
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="wrap prose">
        <p class="eyebrow">British Columbia</p>
        <h1 class="display">Who pays</h1>
        <p>
          In BC, responsibility often splits between the strata corporation (common property, some building systems) and
          the owner (the strata lot, some fixtures), subject to bylaws, the Strata Property Act, deductibles, and
          chargebacks. That split is a legal question.
        </p>
        <p>
          We document what was wet, what we did, and what the log says. We do not decide who writes the cheque. [CLIENT
          — must be reviewed by counsel in this jurisdiction. This page is general guidance and is not legal advice.]
        </p>
        <p>
          New York uses condo, co-op, HO-6, and board language. That copy is not this page. Do not share this text
          across markets.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</MarketLayout>
